register_gate "tests/test_pr_files_pagination.py" "PR FILES PAGINATION GATE: PASS" "pr-files pagination shortfall (a short-but-200 intermediate page no longer silently drops files and produces a false clear)" "pr-files pagination shortfall: the PR Files API is paginated with Link: rel=next termination (primary) + a count-cross-check backstop; a returned<declared shortfall withholds the verdict as honest-unknown instead of releasing lanes on an incomplete file set" "P1 false-clear fix: list_pr_files / list_pr_files_with_ranges previously terminated on len(page)<100, so a proxy/CDN/GitHub edge serving a SHORT but HTTP-200 intermediate page silently ended the loop early and dropped the remaining files. The PR was then analyzed against an incomplete changed-file set, and reconcile_change_claims released lanes for the dropped files -- a real collision on a dropped file went to a FALSE clear. Primary fix: terminate on Link: rel=next (the authoritative GitHub paging signal) via _api_with_link. Backstop: cross-check total returned file-entry count against pull_request.changed_files; a shortfall raises PRFilesShortfall and the caller withholds the verdict as honest-unknown (no reconcile, no lane release), mirroring the suspect_empty_files path. Genuine small PRs (returned==declared) and full multi-page reads still verdict normally." 20
